{
 "answer": "the tilt is not merely dear, it is wrong. On the primary panel the arm with the largest gross gate-specific residual is voltarget at -175 bp/yr -- still negative before any toll -- and the highest break-even belongs to binary_low at -20.583 bp per unit of turnover: below zero, so the gross rule loses before it is charged anything, and 4 of 4 gated arms are in that same state. (Those are two different arms, which is the point: ranking by residual and ranking by break-even do not name the same rule once every arm is below zero.) The equal-weight basket is the one place a root lands above the model cost (binary_low at 37.383 bp/unit), but at 13.041bp that arm's excess is 1.8 bp/yr at t=0.01: it survives the toll by standing at zero after a null arm that lost -689 bp/yr, not by earning, so 0 of 1 survivors clear the bar. Execution cannot rescue a rule whose gross is below the drift it is charged",
